  <section class="bg-bg-secondary py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="h2-section text-center text-text-body">Install. Configure. Verify.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-center text-text-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Three steps: add optimization to your server, set the options you want, and check the
        response headers.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="text-5xl font-bold text-interactive font-mono">1</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-text-body">Install</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
            A native module for your existing web server.
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded">apt install</code> the signed <code
              class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded">mod-pagespeed</code
            > (Apache) or <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded"
              >nginx-module-pagespeed</code
            > (nginx) — prebuilt, nothing to compile. The optimizer worker installs alongside as
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded">pagespeed-optimizer</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="text-5xl font-bold text-interactive font-mono">2</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-text-body">Tell it what to optimize</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
            Same configuration directives as open-source mod_pagespeed. Your existing
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded">pagespeed.conf</code>
            carries over. Enable filters, set the cache path, done.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="text-5xl font-bold text-interactive font-mono">3</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-text-body">Check the response headers</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono"
              >curl -I your-site | grep X-Mod-Pagespeed</code
            >. The version string confirms the module is active; the worker optimizes off the
            request path and serves come from the cache.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

